{"name":"Tantalise","hex":"#669ccb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tantalise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Non-Oxford British English standard spelling of tantalize."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tantalise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tantalus","blocks":[{"text":"Tantalus, was a Greek mythological figure, most famous for his punishment in Tartarus: for either revealing many secrets of the gods, for stealing ambrosia from them, or for trying to trick them into eating his son, he was made to stand in a pool of water beneath a fruit tree with low branches, with the fruit ever eluding his grasp, and the water always receding before he could take a drink. This punishment, although the best-known today, was a more unusual detail in surviving early Greek sources, where variants including a stone suspended above his head are more commonly recorded."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Underworld_Painter_-_RVAp_18-282_-_underworld_-_youth_and_man_in_naiskos_-_M%C3%BCnchen_AS_SH_3297_-_09.jpg/330px-Underworld_Painter_-_RVAp_18-282_-_underworld_-_youth_and_man_in_naiskos_-_M%C3%BCnchen_AS_SH_3297_-_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tantalus"},{"title":"Cynthia Leitich Smith","blocks":[{"text":"Cynthia Leitich Smith is an American author of fiction for children and young adults. A citizen of the Muscogee Nation, her fiction centers on the lives of modern-day Native Americans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cynthia_Leitich_SMith.jpg/330px-Cynthia_Leitich_SMith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cynthia_Leitich_Smith"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Henryk_Siemiradzki_-_Orfeusz_w_podziemnym_kr%C3%B3lestwie.jpg/500px-Henryk_Siemiradzki_-_Orfeusz_w_podziemny